From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:43:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix fundamental bug: live bot's RSI was computed per-minute,
 not per-day like the validated backtest

Live trade history today showed RELIANCE, HDFCBANK, TCS and others
being bought and sold multiple times within 4-10 minutes, repeatedly,
all day - a pattern completely inconsistent with mean_reversion's
actual validated behavior (363 trades total across 15 stocks over
5 YEARS - roughly 5 trades per stock per year).

Root cause: STRATEGY_EVALUATION.md's p=0.0008 result was computed on
"5-year daily data" - RSI(14) there means 14 TRADING DAYS. But the
live tick loop called strategy.decide() on every tick (as often as
every 60 seconds), and MeanReversionStrategy.decide() appends every
price it receives straight into its own rolling window before
computing RSI - so live, RSI(14) was actually a 14-MINUTE indicator.
Same formula, completely different and never-statistically-tested
timeframe. This fully explains both the rapid whipsaw trading (a
14-minute RSI swings through oversold/overbought far more often than
a 14-day one) and the real losses being seen (transaction costs get
paid on every one of those round trips, at a frequency the backtest
never accounted for). The p=0.0008 statistical claim never actually
applied to what was running live.

Fix: added is_decision_time() - restricts actual strategy.decide()
calls to a ~10 minute window near market close (15:20-15:30 IST), once
per symbol per day (tracked via self.last_decision_date). Live price is
still fetched and recorded (PriceTick) every tick as before, for
dashboard display - only the strategy's actual decision-making (and
therefore its internal RSI history) is now gated to genuinely receive
one price per trading day, matching daily-close granularity.

Verified this matches the backtest's own actual cadence:
app/backtest/engine.py's `for tick in prices:` loop calls
strategy.decide() once per entry in `prices`, which
fetch_historical_closes() populates as one close per day - i.e., the
backtest's stop-loss check was ALSO only ever evaluated once per day,
not intraday. This fix makes live behavior consistent with that, not
a new limitation.

Tested: is_decision_time() correctly identifies the close-window vs
market-open-but-too-early vs after-close vs weekend cases. Separately
simulated 5 ticks landing within the same day's decision window and
confirmed exactly 1 decision fires (not 5), with a fresh decision
correctly allowed the next trading day. All 17 existing tests still
pass.

Also noted but not yet cleaned up: app/data_feed/feeds.py already has
its own separate (unused/stub) AngelLiveFeed class, which is now
shadowed by the AngelLiveFeed class added directly in this file
earlier this session. Functionally harmless (Python uses the later
definition) but should be cleaned up as dead/duplicate code.
